"CR6"><label>6.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kozlenkov</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Manes</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Hoylaerts</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name><name><surname>Mill&#x000e1;n</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Function assignment to conserved residues in mammalian alkaline phosphatases</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>2002</year><volume>277</volume><fpage>22992</fpage><lpage>22999</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1074/jbc.M202298200</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Kozlenkov A, Manes T, Hoylaerts MF, Mill&#x000e1;n JL. Function assignment to conserved residues in mammalian alkaline phosphatases. J Biol Chem 2002; 277: 22992&#x02013;9. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11937510</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR7"><label>7.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mornet</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Stura</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Lia-Baldini</surname><given-names>AS</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Structural evidence for a functional role of human tissue nonspecific alkaline phosphatase in bone mineralization</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>2001</year><volume>276</volume><fpage>31171</fpage><lpage>31178</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1074/jbc.M102788200</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Mornet E, Stura E, Lia-Baldini AS et al. Structural evidence for a functional role of human tissue nonspecific alkaline phosphatase in bone mineralization. J Biol Chem 2001; 276: 31171&#x02013;8. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11395499</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR8"><label>8.</label><citation citation-type="other">Hoylaerts MF, Ding L, Narisawa S