6</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR11"><label>11.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hoylaerts</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name><name><surname>Manes</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Mill&#x000e1;n</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Molecular mechanism of uncompetitive inhibition of human placental and germ-cell alkaline phosphatase</article-title><source>Biochem J</source><year>1992</year><volume>286</volume><fpage>23</fpage><lpage>30</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Hoylaerts MF, Manes T, Mill&#x000e1;n JL. Molecular mechanism of uncompetitive inhibition of human placental and germ-cell alkaline phosphatase. Biochem J 1992; 286: 23&#x02013;30. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1520273</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR12"><label>12.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kozlenkov</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Du</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name><name><surname>Cuniasse</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Residues determining the binding specificity of uncompetitive inhibitors to tissue-nonspecific alkaline phosphatase</article-title><source>J Bone Miner Res</source><year>2004</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>1862</fpage><lpage>1872</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1359/JBMR.040608</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Kozlenkov A, Le Du MH, Cuniasse P et al. Residues determining the binding specificity of uncompetitive inhibitors to tissue-nonspecific alkaline phosphatase. J Bone Miner Res 2004; 19: 1862&#x02013;72. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15476587</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR13"><label>13.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bossi</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Hoylaerts</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name><name><surname>Mill&#x000e1;n</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Modifications in a flexible surface loop modulate the isozyme-specific properties of mammalian alkaline phosphatases</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>1993</year><volume>268</volume><fpage>25409</fpage><lpage>25416</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Bossi M, Hoylaerts MF, Mill&#x000e1;n JL. Modifications in a flexible surface loop modulate the isozyme-specific properties of mammalian alkaline phosphatases. J Biol Chem 1993; 268: 25409&#x02013;16. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8244974</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hoylaerts</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name><name><surname>Manes</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Mill&#x000e1;n</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mammalian alkaline phosphatases are allosteric enzymes</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>1997</year><volume>272</volume><fpage>22781</fpage><lpage>22787</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1074/jbc.272.36.22781</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Hoylaerts MF, Manes T, Mill&#x000e1;n JL. Mammalian alkaline phosphatases are allosteric enzymes. J Biol Chem 1997; 272: 22781&#x02013;7. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9278439</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><label>15.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tsonis</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>Argraves</surname><given-names>WS</given-names></name><name><surname>Mill&#x000e1;n</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A putative functional domain of human placental alkaline phosph